==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Aileron (PSF).png|thumb|right|Drawing of an airplane wing showing the aileron.]]

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|aileron|lang=en}}, diminutive of {{m|fr|aile||wing}}, also refers to the extremities of a bird's wings used to control their flight. It first appeared in print in the 7th edition of Cassell's French-English Dictionary of 1877, with its lead meaning of "small wing". In the context of powered airplanes it appears in print about 1908, in the French aviation journal ''L'Aérophile''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The hinged part on the trailing edge of an [[airplane]] [[wing]], used to control [[lateral]] turns.
# A half gable, as at the end of a [[penthouse]] or of the [[aisle]] of a [[church]].

